Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Neutrino incomplete decoupling options", "Subsubsection",ExpressionUUID->"939f27ba-f725-4a91-9139-1f3536487df1"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"$IncompleteNeutrinoDecoupling", "=", "True"}], ";"}], 
  RowBox[{"(*", 
   RowBox[{"Recommended", " ", "True"}], "*)"}]}]], "Input",
 InitializationCell->True,
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.851675837660387*^9, 3.851675838354813*^9}, {
  3.851675913891988*^9, 3.8516759210669203`*^9}, {3.851675972032069*^9, 
  3.851675974223915*^9}, {3.9350346179749937`*^9, 3.935034620897367*^9}, {
  3.9351239954491367`*^9, 3.935123995855268*^9}, {3.935125517375978*^9, 
  3.935125517929686*^9}, {3.935543700066148*^9, 3.93554370058307*^9}, {
  3.93557528765665*^9, 3.935575288331416*^9}, {3.935575683172379*^9, 
  3.935575683585578*^9}, {3.935576208077668*^9, 3.9355762085976458`*^9}, {
  3.935576608356686*^9, 3.935576608746809*^9}, {3.935577295579443*^9, 
  3.9355772964077377`*^9}, {3.9355837377999268`*^9, 3.935583738156097*^9}, {
  3.935651423450037*^9, 3.935651423982836*^9}, {3.935980393672571*^9, 
  3.935980394141101*^9}},
 CellLabel->"In[97]:=",ExpressionUUID->"8541dc67-bc41-4f80-ac05-5e6f05f11391"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "If $IncompleteNeutrinoDecoupling is set to True, the entropy transfer from ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox["e", "\[PlusMinus]"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "45f3ac59-d71b-478e-9e51-680675f600f1"],
 " annihilations to neutrinos is taken into account. Indeed if we consider \
the details of the decoupling of neutrinos, it is found that decoupling is \
incomplete by the time electrons and positrons annihilate into photons. This \
results in a slight overheating of neutrinos and cooling of the \
electrons/photons plasma.\nThe advised value for \
$IncompleteNeutrinoDecoupling is True."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"f59e5b0b-adfb-4848-9c6c-fb787314edf8"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"$NEVO", "=", "True"}], ";"}], " ", 
  RowBox[{"(*", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Recommended", " ", "True"}], " ", "*)"}]}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"$TrueT\[Nu]e", "=", "True"}], ";"}], 
  RowBox[{"(*", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Recommended", " ", "True"}], " ", "*)"}], 
  " "}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"$FileSuffix", "=", "\"\<\>\""}], ";"}], 
  RowBox[{"(*", 
   RowBox[{
   "Suffix", " ", "of", " ", "the", " ", "file", " ", "name", " ", "in", " ", 
    "which", " ", "NEVO", " ", "results", " ", "are", " ", 
    RowBox[{"stored", "."}]}], " ", "*)"}]}]}], "Input",
 InitializationCell->True,
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.8612595957967587`*^9, 3.86125959672474*^9}, {
  3.861261718541793*^9, 3.861261719004272*^9}, {3.934958598002645*^9, 
  3.934958602900876*^9}, {3.93512426372217*^9, 3.935124275318284*^9}, {
  3.935124984424987*^9, 3.935124985018446*^9}, {3.9351252820965767`*^9, 
  3.9351252824944696`*^9}, {3.935576224777947*^9, 3.935576227946849*^9}, {
  3.9355766103233137`*^9, 3.9355766129508877`*^9}, {3.93619021565384*^9, 
  3.9361902475964727`*^9}, {3.9889329635484667`*^9, 3.988932964116724*^9}, {
  3.98893347816885*^9, 3.988933478621016*^9}},
 CellLabel->"In[98]:=",ExpressionUUID->"aac143ed-baab-47c1-93a4-4ab82afab28d"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The original PRIMAT approach consisted in using a fit for the heating \
function of the neutrinos due to incomplete decoupling. The fitting functions \
which is used is the one given in [PArthENoPE]. It is used in Eq. 63 of the \
companion paper. In this approach, all three flavors of neutrinos have \
equilibrium distributions at a common temperature derived in Eq. 64 of the \
companion paper. This original method is chosen if $NEVO = False.\n\nHowever, \
if $NEVO is set to True, we directly import the neutrino effective \
temperatures (and the heating function) from the results obtained with NEVO, \
a Python code designed to implement neutrino evolution through the MeV age \
(developed by Julien Froustey and Cyril Pitrou, and described in [Froustey et \
al. 2020]). This enables to take into account two additional effects: the \
different decoupling of electron and muon/tau neutrinos, resulting in \
different effective temperatures (implemented if $TrueT\[Nu]e is set to True) \
and non-thermal distortions of the neutrinos distribution functions \
(implemented if $SpectralDistortions is set to True, see below).\n\n",
 StyleBox["Important:",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " it would be inconsistent to set $SpectralDistortions = True but \
$IncompleteNeutrinoDecoupling = False, except if the are analytic distortions \
included (see below). That is why when computing the weak rates, spectral \
distortions are included only if both these options are set to True, or if \
$AnalyticDistortions is set to True.\nThe code checks for most obvious \
inconsistent options and modifies them (printing a warning message)\n\nThe \
common neutrino average temperature can therefore be computed in two \
different (but, in principle, equivalent) ways: \n1/ through the heating \
function \n2/ directly from the effective temperatures. \nIf $Taverage\
\[ScriptCapitalN] is set to True, the first method is used but we prefer the \
second method, hence we set it to False."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.934958655590507*^9, 3.9349586562887373`*^9}, {
  3.9351057867204037`*^9, 3.9351057872618113`*^9}, {3.935574516306354*^9, 
  3.9355745527379427`*^9}, {3.937273174495028*^9, 3.937273174998392*^9}, {
  3.9372734205974073`*^9, 3.9372734236645327`*^9}, {3.9372734842521048`*^9, 
  3.937273508807068*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"c0bd8283-f157-4463-bbc0-\
701179458828"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"$Taverage\[ScriptCapitalN]", "=", "False"}], ";"}], 
  RowBox[{"(*", 
   RowBox[{"Recommended", " ", "False"}], " ", "*)"}]}]], "Input",
 InitializationCell->True,
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.8612603029544983`*^9, 3.861260303433213*^9}, {
  3.861261729743487*^9, 3.861261730337091*^9}},
 CellLabel->
  "In[101]:=",ExpressionUUID->"aac143ed-baab-47c1-93a4-4ab82afab28d"],

Cell["Files in which NEVO results are stored", "Text",
